---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE_URL, SITE_NAME, CONTACT } from '../site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The terms under which you may use WorldFreightHub: the informational nature of the data, rate disclaimers, acceptable use and liability limits."
  canonical={`${SITE_URL}/terms-of-use/`}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Terms of Use' }]} />
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        These terms apply to your use of {SITE_NAME} ({SITE_URL}). By using the
        site you accept them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section container">
    <h2>1. What this site is</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is a freight information reference covering the China–GCC
      corridor. It is <strong>not</strong> a freight forwarder, carrier,
      customs broker or legal advisor. Nothing on this site constitutes an
      offer to carry goods, a quotation, or professional advice.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Rates and data are estimates</h2>
    <p>
      All freight rates, transit times, duty, VAT and cost figures on this site
      are <strong>indicative reference estimates</strong>, clearly labelled
      HIGH / MEDIUM / LOW confidence where data quality permits. Rates move
      constantly with fuel, season and geopolitical risk. Always confirm
      figures with a licensed carrier or customs broker before making
      commercial decisions. See the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>
      and <a href="/data-changelog/">data changelog</a> for how figures are
      produced and updated.
    </p>

    <h2>3. No liability for decisions based on site data</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep information accurate and source-backed, but we make no
      warranty that any figure is current at the moment you read it. To the
      extent permitted by law, {SITE_NAME} and its operator are not liable for
      losses arising from reliance on site information, including shipping
      delays, customs penalties, price differences or missed commercial
      opportunities.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Third-party providers and external links</h2>
    <p>
      The directory lists freight providers, and quote requests are routed to
      providers on your selected corridor. Any engagement between you and a
      provider — pricing, carriage, insurance, disputes — is a contract
      between you and that provider. External links to port authorities,
      customs authorities and other sources are provided for reference; we do
      not control their content.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Do not scrape, republish or resell site data at scale without permission.</li>
      <li>Do not use the quote form to send spam or false requests.</li>
      <li>Do not attempt to disrupt site availability.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      Site text, tables and data compilations are the property of the operator
      unless a third-party source is attributed. Short quotations with a link
      to the page are permitted.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Errors should be reported through the
      <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>; we review and record every
      correction on the <a href="/data-changelog/">data changelog</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms. Continued use after an update means
      acceptance of the revised terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms:
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>
    </p>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 19 September 2026</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
